{
	"version": 5,
	"rows": [
		{
			"id": "eXaA7ExXZHcS8JGFR",
			"description": "Power Sword, Drukhari Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Field-on line carries armour divisor (10), per the framework's power-field rule.\n\nLore: The disruption-field blade of the Drukhari elite: Archons, Succubi and Sybarites carry power swords as symbols of rank as much as weapons (Codex: Drukhari background). It is the same weapon in principle as an Imperial or Aeldari power sword, built with the barbed, cruel styling of Commorragh.\n\nDesign: Built on the power-field rule exactly: mundane blade sw+1 cut (field off), field on adds +3d and armour divisor (10), sw+3d+1(10) cut, the same as every other power sword in the project since the disruption field does not care who forged the blade. Exact dice at an Archon's ST 12 (sw 1d+2, so 4d+3 with the field on): penetrates flak 100.0%, carapace 99.9%, Astartes plate (effective 10) 97.3% and Terminator plate (effective 19) 23.9% (24.3% with the WP chance). At a Kabalite's ST 10 (sw 1d, so 4d+1) the figures are 100.0/98.8/90.3/9.7%: a Kabalite officer can still cut down a Marine, but not a Terminator. Handling: 3.5 lb, a little heavier than the Aeldari pattern's 3 lb for its barbed, more elaborate guard, min ST 10 (the Aeldari weapon is ST 9), reach 1, parry 0, Broadsword.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari",
				"Kabal",
				"Wych Cult"
			],
