		{
			"id": "egIrh25jVRgCWmYgV",
			"description": "Huskblade",
			"local_notes": "Field-on line carries armour divisor (10). The follow-up line is used only with the field on (the drain is carried by the disruption field).\n\nLore: A power sword particular to Archons that, in Codex: Drukhari background, drains the vitality of what it wounds, leaving a dried husk. It is a personal weapon of the Kabal's greatest lords and is not carried by their warriors.\n\nDesign: Built on the power-field rule (framework: 'power-field rule plus a follow-up'): mundane sw+2 cut, field on adds +3d (sw+3d+2(10) cut), one point over the standard Drukhari power sword to reflect a master-crafted lord's weapon, plus a 2d tox follow-up (average 7) if the blade penetrates, representing the desiccating drain. Exact dice at an Archon's ST 12 (4d+4 field on): flak 100.0%, carapace 100.0%, Astartes plate 98.8%, Terminator plate 33.6% (33.9% with WP 3). The follow-up is small in Space Marine terms (HP 34) but ends most human-scale targets. Handling: 4 lb, min ST 10, reach 1, parry 0, Broadsword.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari",
				"Kabal"
			],
			"tech_level": "11^",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "16000",
			"base_weight": "4 lb",
