		{
			"id": "e-TOEu1PwL_XguOG8",
			"description": "Incubus Demiklaives (pair)",
			"local_notes": "Field-on line carries armour divisor (10). Sold and weighed as a pair; each blade is a one-handed weapon. Fighting with both blades gives two attacks a turn, the second at the usual off-hand penalty unless the wielder is Ambidextrous; each blade parries separately.\n\nLore: A pair of shorter one-handed power blades carried by Incubi who fight with two weapons rather than one (Codex: Drukhari background). The paired blades give up reach and raw power for speed, in line with the Incubi's role as elite duellists.\n\nDesign: Each blade uses the standard Drukhari power-field line, sw+3d+1(10) cut (field off sw+1), at 3 lb apiece. Exact dice at ST 12: 4d+3(10), so flak 100.0%, carapace 99.9%, Astartes plate 97.3%, Terminator plate 23.9% per blade: half the klaive's 44.4% on the toughest armour, the price for two blades and two attacks. Handling: 3 lb each (6 lb the pair), min ST 10 each, reach 1, parry 0, Shortsword.",
