		{
			"id": "ejoz5XGWv-_8aTN7H",
			"description": "Agoniser (Blade)",
			"local_notes": "Field-on line carries armour divisor (10). Agony follow-up: if the field-on strike penetrates DR, roll HT-3 or suffer Severe Pain (-4 to all IQ- and DX-based rolls, B428) for a number of minutes equal to the margin of failure; a critical failure also stuns the victim. High Pain Threshold gives +3 to the roll (GM's call for other pain resistance). No effect on machines or on anything that does not feel pain.\n\nLore: The bladed form of the agoniser, favoured by Archons and by Succubi who want a duelling weapon: a short blade whose field, as with the whip, overloads the nerves rather than shears the flesh (Codex: Drukhari background).\n\nDesign: Same principle as the whip: a field weapon (10) whose real weapon is the pain affliction. A blade can carry a little more damage than a whip: sw+1d+1(10) cut (2d+3 at a Succubus's ST 12), still 2d under the power sword's +3d. Exact dice at ST 12: flak 100.0%, carapace 83.3%, Astartes plate 41.7% (42.7% with WP 4), Terminator plate 0.0% (0.3% with WP 3): a duellist's weapon that reaches through carapace far more reliably than a whip but is no threat to Terminators. Handling: 3 lb, min ST 8, reach 1, parry 0, Shortsword.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari",
				"Wych Cult",
				"Haemonculus Coven",
				"Kabal"
			],
