		{
			"id": "eihb_VB-H8djV_uNp",
			"description": "Wych Hydra Gauntlets (pair)",
			"local_notes": "Worn as a pair: the Wych may attack with both in one turn (second attack at the usual off-hand penalty unless she is Ambidextrous). Parry uses Brawling/2+3 as for any hand weapon. Blades are hyper-keen Commorraghan edges (armour divisor (3)), not a power field.\n\nLore: Clawed gauntlets worn by Hekatrixes and Wyches: a pair of hand-blades bonded to the forearm that let a Wych rake, slash and parry at close quarters with tremendous speed (Codex: Drukhari background). Wych weapons are consistently shown as monofilament-sharp rather than power-field weapons; the tabletop gives them armour penetration but no field, and that is the reading used here.\n\nDesign: No framework anchor beyond 'mundane weapons made lethal by the Wych's skill; no power fields'. The edge is set by the same reasoning as the Aeldari shuriken (monomolecular edge, divisor (3)) and the Imperial chainsword (sw+2d(2)): a hyper-sharp edge with no motor or field gets the shuriken's (3) at the chainsword's two extra dice, sw+2d(3) cut. Exact dice at a Wych's ST 11 (sw 1d+1, so 3d+1(3), average 11.5): penetrates flak (effective 10) 62.5% of hits (68.5% with the Weak Points chance), carapace (effective 23.3) 0.0% (2.3% with WP 5) and Astartes plate 0.0% (0.1% with WP 4). Flak is therefore a coin-flip-plus for each blow, which with a Wych's many attacks a turn is how she butchers Guardsmen, while carapace and power armour still turn her aside except on gaps. Handling: 3 lb the pair, min ST 8, reach C,1, parry 0, Brawling. TL 10 with the ^ mark for the Commorragh edge.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari",
				"Wych Cult"
			],
			"tech_level": "10^",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "3000",
			"base_weight": "3 lb",
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "we3cDTxZlDAp6YRRb",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "cut",
						"st": "sw",
						"base": "2d",
						"armor_divisor": 3
					},
					"reach": "C,1",
					"parry": "0",
					"strength": "8",
					"usage": "Claw strike, each gauntlet",
					"defaults": [
						{
							"type": "dx",
							"modifier": 0
						},
						{
							"type": "skill",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Brawling"
							}
						}
					]
				}
			],
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "elWlz625XS9sxfw81",
			"description": "Razorflails (pair)",
			"local_notes": "Ordinary flail rules apply: the U in 0U means the flail is unbalanced (it cannot parry after it has attacked that turn), and a defender's parry against a flail is at -4. Carried as a pair.\n\nLore: A pair of chain-flails studded with razor-edged blades, favoured by Wyches who fight at a range that makes a blade user's guard difficult (Codex: Drukhari background). The arena fighters use them in a whirling, almost dancing style; the edges are Commorragh-keen, not power-field.\n\nDesign: Same edge reasoning as the hydra gauntlets: a razor-bladed chain flail is a cutting weapon with a monomolecular-class edge, sw+2d(3) cut, kept at reach 1,2 and parry 0U (framework: flails 0U). Exact dice at a Wych's ST 11 (3d+1(3)): flak 62.5% (68.5% with Weak Points), carapace 0.0% (2.3%), Astartes 0.0% (0.1%). What the flail adds over the gauntlets is reach and the -4 to parry it. Handling: 2.5 lb each (5 lb the pair), min ST 9, reach 1,2, parry 0U, Flail.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari",
				"Wych Cult"
			],
			"tech_level": "10^",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "2800",
			"base_weight": "5 lb",
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "wPlPwWV2hw1p7WHzT",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "cut",
						"st": "sw",
