		{
			"id": "eeWMNlCQbkylgW3v7",
			"description": "Shardnet and Impaler",
			"local_notes": "The impaler is used one-handed while the net is held, or two-handed for the thr line's usual reach. Roughly a gladiator's trident-and-net kit.\n\nLore: The arena kit of the Wych Cult's net-and-spear fighters: a crystal-studded net to bind an opponent and a barbed trident or spear to finish them (Codex: Drukhari background, Wych arena weapons). The impaler's head is a Commorragh-keen point; the net is unchanged.\n\nDesign: Two weapons in one item. The impaler is a spear-class thrusting weapon with the same hyper-keen edge as the other Wych blades, thr+2d(3) imp (the shuriken's (3), two extra dice over the thrust as for the flail and gauntlets), reach 1,2*, min ST 9. Exact dice at a Wych's ST 11 (thr 1d-1, so 3d-1(3), average 9.5): flak 37.5% (46.7% with WP), carapace 0.0% (1.2%), Astartes 0.0%. Thrusts are weaker than swings against armour because thr is lower than sw at this ST, but the impaling wound multiplier makes each penetrating hit hurt. The shardnet is unchanged: thrown (range 3/6, ST 8, 3 lb), Binding rather than damage, to bring the target down to a defenceless state for the impaler. Handling: 4 lb impaler + 3 lb net, min ST 9 and 8.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari",
				"Wych Cult"
			],
			"tech_level": "10^",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "2200",
			"base_weight": "7 lb",
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "wxGBMaHomaz7RmIed",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "imp",
						"st": "thr",
						"base": "2d",
						"armor_divisor": 3
					},
					"reach": "1,2*",
					"parry": "0",
					"strength": "9",
					"usage": "Impaler, thrust",
					"defaults": [
						{
							"type": "dx",
							"modifier": -5
						},
						{
							"type": "skill",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Polearm"
							},
							"modifier": -4
						},
						{
							"type": "skill",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Staff"
							},
							"modifier": -2
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "W1xH6G7FKSORl-Gp6",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "spec"
					},
					"accuracy": "0",
					"range": "3/6",
					"rate_of_fire": "1",
					"shots": "1(T)",
					"bulk": "-3",
					"strength": "8",
					"usage": "Shardnet, thrown",
					"usage_notes": "A hit entangles the target: Binding (advantage, ST 12, DR 2). While bound, each turn spent struggling the wire and crystals cut for 1d cut (no attack roll). Recovering a thrown net takes 1d turns and the Wych's next Ready. Cannot parry while it is thrown.",
					"defaults": [
						{
							"type": "dx",
							"modifier": -6
						}
					]
				}
			],
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "exmWKKC-bh2tr4lbN",
			"description": "Wych Blade",
			"local_notes": "Also stands for the shorter Wych knife: use the same profile at reach C,1 if the GM wants a concealed dagger.\n\nLore: The basic close-combat blade of the Wych Cults, carried by Wyches as a side-arm alongside more specialised weapons. The sources do not give it a distinct canonical profile; this entry is built to give Wych characters an ordinary Commorraghan blade.\n\nDesign: A shortsword-class blade with the Commorragh hyper-keen edge: one die over the plain sword's sw / thr+1 and the (3) divisor, sw+1d(3) cut and thr+1d(3) imp (a lighter blade than the gauntlets and flails, so one die of edge rather than two). Exact dice at a Wych's ST 11: the swing (2d+1(3), average 8) penetrates flak 16.7% (27.9% with WP), carapace 0.0% (0.4%), Astartes 0.0%; the thrust (2d-1(3)) 2.8% flak (12.0% with WP). It cuts ordinary clothing and light armour readily and only worries flak on a lucky roll. Handling: 1.5 lb, min ST 7, reach 1, parry 0, Shortsword.",
