		{
			"id": "efbTD6rn42-o13o0P",
			"description": "Scissorhand",
			"local_notes": "Two blades pivoting on a joint like shears. A Haemonculus with a scissorhand on each arm may attack with both, the second at the usual off-hand penalty unless Ambidextrous.\n\nLore: A giant pair of shears worn as a glove or bonded to the arm by Haemonculi and used as surgical and torture implements (Codex: Drukhari background gives a scissorhand as a Haemonculus's melee weapon). Its shear-edges are Commorragh-keen.\n\nDesign: No framework anchor; a mundane heavy cutting weapon with the hyper-keen edge used across the Drukhari blades: sw+1d(3) cut, no field. Exact dice at a Haemonculus's ST 13 (sw 2d-1, so 3d-1(3), average 9.5): flak 37.5% (46.7% with WP 7), carapace 0.0% (1.2% with WP 5), Astartes 0.0%. A surgeon's tool that goes through a flak jacket about as often as not. Handling: 4 lb, min ST 11, reach 1, parry 0.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari",
				"Haemonculus Coven"
			],
			"tech_level": "10^",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "3500",
			"base_weight": "4 lb",
