		{
			"id": "eXt7t17VZ-vQlTWrw",
			"description": "Flesh Gauntlet",
			"local_notes": "Grown, not built: the gauntlet is fused into the wearer's arm by surgery. Removing or replacing it takes a Haemonculus (Surgery roll). The crushing damage is mundane; the toxin is the sting.\n\nLore: A brutish grafted gauntlet used by Haemonculi as a melee weapon (Codex: Drukhari background). The sources say little about its exact working, so it is built as a heavy gauntlet with a coven toxin follow-up, a design choice consistent with the Haemonculus's trade.\n\nDesign: No framework anchor; a heavy fist-weapon of the Basic Set type, kept mundane as the coordinator asked: thr+3 cr at a Haemonculus's ST 13 (thr 1d, so 1d+3, average 6.5), no divisor, so it penetrates flak 0.0% and the toxin never fires against armour; against bare flesh it adds 2d tox (average 7). That makes it a weapon for unarmoured victims, the surgeon's usual subjects. Handling: 5 lb, min ST 10, reach C,1, parry 0, Brawling.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari",
				"Haemonculus Coven"
			],
			"tech_level": "10^",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "3500",
			"base_weight": "5 lb",
			"weapons": [
