		{
			"id": "ex65jGBVJkytDoNNA",
			"description": "Glimmersteel Blade",
			"local_notes": "Mundane: no power field and no follow-up; the (3) divisor is the keenness of the metal, not a field.\n\nLore: The blade of the Mandrake, a shadow-steel weapon carried into fights from the darkness (Codex: Drukhari background gives Mandrakes a glimmersteel blade). Sources describe it as exceptionally keen; no detailed profile is given.\n\nDesign: No framework anchor. An exotic alloy that holds a molecular-fine edge: the same sw+1d(3) cut and thr+1d(3) imp as the Wych blade (the shuriken's (3), one die over a plain sword), but with better min ST and cost for the alloy. Exact dice at a Mandrake's ST 11 (sw 1d+1): swing 2d+1(3) penetrates flak 16.7% (27.9% with WP), carapace 0.0% (0.4%), Astartes 0.0%; thrust 2d-1(3) flak 2.8% (12.0%). It rewards a Mandrake's stealth: an ambush strike on the unarmoured throat, not a slugfest with plate. Handling: 2 lb, min ST 8, reach 1, parry 0, Shortsword.",
