		{
			"id": "efxDRhQJCJLUdQ9Le",
			"description": "Venom Blade",
			"local_notes": "Mundane blade with a hollow edge fed from a poison reservoir.\n\nLore: A poisoned blade carried by Archons and by some Kabal elites such as the winged Scourges as a close-range weapon (Codex: Drukhari background; the pairing with Scourges I hold with less certainty). The Drukhari's penchant for toxins makes it a natural companion to the splinter weapons.\n\nDesign: Not a power weapon: a sword-class blade with the Commorragh hyper-keen edge and a poison follow-up, the melee counterpart of the splinter rifle's toxin. Swing sw+1d(3) cut, thrust thr+1d(3) imp. Exact dice at an Archon's ST 12 (sw 1d+2): swing 2d+2(3) penetrates flak 27.8% (38.5% with WP 7), carapace 0.0% (0.8%), Astartes 0.0%; thrust 2d-1(3) flak 2.8% (12.0%). The edge gets through flak on a good roll; when it does, the 3d tox follow-up (average 10.5) is what kills. Handling: 3 lb, min ST 9, reach 1, parry 0, Broadsword.",
